  "codex_last_message": "Implemented a real lazy-build 2-level IVF baseline in [src/db.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/db.rs) with AVX-512 distance kernels in [src/distance.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/distance.rs). Bulk inserts now just buffer vectors; the first search builds the hierarchy, and timed queries use primary-centroid shortlist selection, secondary-cluster refinement, then exact rerank over shortlisted vectors. I also added a small harness helper at [.meta_codex/tools/summarize_benchmarks](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/summarize_benchmarks) and updated the campaign state files and journal.\n\nValidation is now in a valid state: `run_correctness_test` passed at `0.9660` recall, and the best local quick benchmark is `3076.50 QPS` at `0.9610` recall on 1000 queries from [benchmark_002.json](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/benchmarks/benchmark_002.json). Current expectation is a stable low-3k-QPS valid solution locally; there is no evidence yet that this cycle is anywhere near the `22000` target. `run_profiling` could not run here because `perf` is not installed.\n\nNext best move: keep the 2-level shortlist architecture, but add a cheap intra-cluster prefilter or compressed code path so exact rerank touches far fewer vectors per query while preserving the current recall margin.",
